{
  "_comment": "Cross-language oracle for the group-membership export. cli/gh-teacher/internal/groupcmd (buildRows + defangCells) and web/src/domain/submissions/groupMembershipCsv.ts (buildGroupMembershipCsvRows) must both reproduce every case's `rows` byte for byte, in `columns` order, and both must map `default_name` inputs to its outputs. `roster_csv` is the raw roster.csv text: each side feeds it through the production reader its export uses (Go configrepo.ParseRosterLenient; web parseCsvRowsStrictWidth plus toStudent), so the oracle also pins how a padded, zero-padded, unparsable, short, or overlong cell reaches the builder and that the two readers admit the same students: a row short by exactly one trailing cell joins, a row short by two or more or carrying surplus cells does not. Members carry an optional GitHub `id`; `fallback: true` marks a member derived from the repository name (a legacy founder) rather than a live read; `members: null` is an unreadable group, `[]` a group with no members yet.",
